    <cosy-teacher-notes type="additional">
      <p><cosy-text type="strong">Teacher&apos;s Linguistic Error Correction Guidance:</cosy-text></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Incorrect: He have went to Paris → Correct: He has gone to Paris ((Underlined error: &apos;have&apos; and auxiliary usage. Correction: Present perfect singular &apos;has&apos; + past participle &apos;gone&apos;))</li>
        <li>Incorrect: We discussed about the problem → Correct: We discussed the problem / had a discussion about the problem ((Underlined prepositional error. Better collocation: &apos;discuss&apos; is transitive and takes no preposition, or use &apos;have a discussion about&apos;))</li>
        <li>Incorrect: His explanation was very clear → Correct: His explanation was exceptionally lucid / crystal clear / coherent ((Elevating vocabulary with highly specific advanced options and sophisticated synonyms))</li>
      </ul>
    </cosy-teacher-notes>
